Subject: [Pico QEMU ABI] Refuse QTEE firmware initialization on the virtual board

QEMU has no Qualcomm TEE shared-memory monitor. Keep the exported API
linked for vendor callers, but do not issue an SMC from its early initcall.
This patch is selected only by the separate QEMU transport variant.

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qtee_shmbridge.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qtee_shmbridge.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/genalloc.h>
@@ -342,6 +343,9 @@
 	uint32_t ns_vm_ids[] = {VMID_HLOS};
 	uint32_t ns_vm_perms[] = {VM_PERM_R|VM_PERM_W};
 
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("linux,dummy-virt"))
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	if (default_bridge.vaddr) {
 		pr_warn("qtee shmbridge is already initialized\n");
 		return 0;
